{"timestamp_utc": "2026-10-06T03:37:44.041534+00:00", "event_type": "request_start", "payload": {"attempt": 2, "stage": "action", "directory": "action", "request": {"model": "qwen3.8-max", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": "Carry out the sealed recipient decision below. Do not inspect hidden tests or external files. Return exactly {\"source_files\":{...}} containing the complete current public snapshot. Change only paths listed in writable_paths and preserve every other path.\nSEALED JUDGMENT:\n{\"decision\": \"accept\", \"confidence\": 0.95, \"target_role\": \"recipient\", \"target_paths\": [], \"defect_type\": \"unknown\", \"evidence_refs\": [\"producer.py:serialize_event\", \"producer.py:produce_events\", \"producer.py:json.dumps(data, default=str)\", \"producer.py:encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\"\"], \"observed_artifact_sha256\": \"1529b41e454f5a1f7c8c48a7366bd50fe58be8c91686e773d3afe9d7afc693a2\", \"repair_plan\": \"No changes needed to producer.py. As recipient, I will ensure processor.py reads the JSONL output from this producer, parses each line back into appropriate structures preserving all event fields including non-ASCII characters, and passes records to the sink in the expected format.\", \"rationale\": \"The delivered producer.py correctly serializes UserEvent objects to JSON lines with all required fields (event_id, timestamp, user_name, action, page_url). It uses json.dumps with default=str for datetime handling and writes with utf-8 encoding to support non-ASCII sample values. The public function signatures (serialize_event, produce_events) are preserved. As the recipient role, I am not authorized to modify producer.py; my responsibility is processor.py. The producer artifact meets the contract requirements.\"}\nACTION PAYLOAD:\n{\"task_id\": \"PIPE3_stream_processing\", \"seed\": 0, \"role\": \"recipient\", \"task_text\": {\"spec_md\": \"# PIPE3: Stream Processing Interoperability\\n\\n## Goal\\nMake the public producer -> processor -> sink pipeline interoperate for the `user_analytics`\\nevent schema and its sample records.\\n\\n## Responsibilities\\n- The producer owns `producer.py` and must preserve its public names and signatures.\\n- The recipient owns `processor.py` and must preserve its public names and signatures.\\n- `models.py` and `sink.py` are read-only support files.\\n\\n## Acceptance\\nThe components must exchange records correctly, preserve the declared event fields,\\nhandle the supplied non-ASCII sample values, and produce output that the public sink\\ncan consume. Keep the patch limited to the contracted files. The parent evaluator keeps\\nits tests private; inspect the public interfaces and data flow before editing.\\n\", \"brief_md\": \"# PIPE3 stream task (user_analytics)\\n\\nRepair the assigned component so the public producer, processor, and sink work together.\\nRead the available source and public interfaces, preserve compatibility, and return only\\nthe complete text of files you are allowed to change.\\n\"}, \"source_files\": {\"processor.py\": \"\\nimport json\\nimport os\\nfrom datetime import datetime\\n\\n\\ndef parse_timestamp(ts_str: str) -> datetime:\\n    \\n    return datetime.fromisoformat(ts_str)\\n\\n\\ndef transform_event(event_data: dict) -> dict:\\n    \\n    processed = dict(event_data)\\n    \\n    ts = parse_timestamp(event_data[\\\"timestamp\\\"])\\n    processed[\\\"timestamp\\\"] = ts.isoformat()\\n    processed[\\\"processed_at\\\"] = datetime.utcnow().isoformat()\\n    processed[\\\"action\\\"] = event_data[\\\"action\\\"].upper()\\n    return processed\\n\\n\\ndef process_events(input_path: str, output_path: str) -> int:\\n    \\n    count = 0\\n    \\n    with open(input_path, \\\"r\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\") as fin,\\\\\\n         open(output_path, \\\"w\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\") as fout:\\n        for line in fin:\\n            line = line.strip()\\n            if not line:\\n                continue\\n            event_data = json.loads(line)\\n            processed = transform_event(event_data)\\n            \\n            fout.write(json.dumps(processed, ensure_ascii=False) + \\\"\\\\n\\\")\\n            count += 1\\n    return count\\n\", \"models.py\": \"\\nfrom __future__ import annotations\\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\\nfrom datetime import datetime\\n\\n\\nVALID_ACTIONS = [\\\"page_view\\\", \\\"click\\\", \\\"scroll\\\", \\\"purchase\\\"]\\n\\n\\n@dataclass\\nclass UserEvent:\\n    \\n    event_id: str\\n    timestamp: datetime\\n    user_name: str\\n    action: str\\n    page_url: str\\n\\n    def validate(self) -> bool:\\n        \\n        if not self.event_id:\\n            raise ValueError(\\\"event_id is required\\\")\\n        if self.action not in VALID_ACTIONS:\\n            raise ValueError(f\\\"Invalid action: {self.action}\\\")\\n        return True\\n\", \"sink.py\": \"\\nimport json\\nimport os\\nfrom datetime import datetime\\n\\n\\ndef load_processed_events(input_path: str) -> list[dict]:\\n    \\n    events = []\\n    with open(input_path, \\\"r\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\") as f:\\n        for line in f:\\n            line = line.strip()\\n            if not line:\\n                continue\\n            event = json.loads(line)\\n            \\n            _ = event[\\\"event_id\\\"]  \\n            _ = event[\\\"timestamp\\\"]\\n            events.append(event)\\n    return events\\n\\n\\ndef write_summary(events: list[dict], output_path: str) -> dict:\\n    \\n    summary = {\\n        \\\"total_events\\\": len(events),\\n        \\\"actions\\\": {},\\n        \\\"users\\\": set(),\\n    }\\n    for evt in events:\\n        action = evt[\\\"action\\\"]\\n        summary[\\\"actions\\\"][action] = summary[\\\"actions\\\"].get(action, 0) + 1\\n        summary[\\\"users\\\"].add(evt[\\\"user_name\\\"])\\n\\n    summary[\\\"unique_users\\\"] = len(summary[\\\"users\\\"])\\n    summary[\\\"users\\\"] = sorted(summary[\\\"users\\\"])\\n\\n    with open(output_path, \\\"w\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\") as f:\\n        json.dump(summary, f, indent=2, ensure_ascii=False)\\n\\n    return summary\\n\", \"producer.py\": \"\\nimport json\\nimport os\\nfrom datetime import datetime\\nfrom models import UserEvent\\n\\n\\ndef serialize_event(event: UserEvent) -> str:\\n    \\n    data = {\\n        \\\"event_id\\\": event.event_id,\\n        \\\"timestamp\\\": event.timestamp,\\n        \\\"user_name\\\": event.user_name,\\n        \\\"action\\\": event.action,\\n        \\\"page_url\\\": event.page_url,\\n    }\\n    \\n    return json.dumps(data, default=str)\\n\\n\\ndef produce_events(events: list[UserEvent], output_path: str) -> None:\\n    \\n    with open(output_path, \\\"w\\\", encoding=\\\"utf-8\\\") as f:\\n        for event in events:\\n            f.write(serialize_event(event) + \\\"\\\\n\\\")\\n\"}, \"writable_paths\": [\"processor.py\"], \"required_delivery_paths\": [], \"ready_for_dispatch\": true, \"delivery_sha256\": \"1529b41e454f5a1f7c8c48a7366bd50fe58be8c91686e773d3afe9d7afc693a2\", \"consumer_action\": \"use\", \"action_initialization\": \"selected_delivery_copy\", \"input_source_sha256\": \"819118801d4ccfab2801b36032d4f0808bdf938eedf9ee532d8ea798fd7ffa29\", \"prior_delivery_may_have_been_seen\": true, \"independent_redo_is_blinded_control\": false}"}], "temperature": 0, "max_tokens": 2048, "stream": true, "thinking": {"type": "disabled"}}, "command_without_secret": ["curl", "-q", "--silent", "--show-error", "--no-buffer", "--fail-with-body", "--noproxy", "*", "--connect-timeout", "15", "--max-time", "300", "--config", "-", "--data-binary", "@/Users/jingwu/work/earning-roles/experiments/logs/n03_c1_pipe3_bounded_live_20261006_v2/contextual_trust_linear/decision_0/action/action_request.json", "--output", "/Users/jingwu/work/earning-roles/experiments/logs/n03_c1_pipe3_bounded_live_20261006_v2/contextual_trust_linear/decision_0/action/action_response.sse", "--write-out", "%{json}", "https://idealab.alibaba-inc.com/api/code/v1/messages"], 